# Story: As a truck driver, I want other drivers to be unable to see my bookings, so that my schedule and containers stay private. When another driver asks for my booking by its reference they are told it does not exist (NOT_FOUND), exactly as for a reference that really does not exist.

@draft
Feature: Booking Privacy

  Scenario Outline: Another driver cannot see my booking details
    Given I am a driver
    And I book that slot for a valid container
    Then the booking is confirmed with a reference "<reference>"
    
    When another driver looks up my booking
    Then they are told it does not exist
    
    Examples:
      | reference |
      | "ABCD1234"|
      | "EFGH5678"|

  Scenario: Booking privacy when slot is full
    Given I am a driver
    And another driver has booked that slot for the same container
    When I book that slot for container "<container>"
    Then the outcome is "SLOT_FULL"
    
    Examples:
      | container |
      | "CONT1234"|
      | "CONT5678"|

  Scenario: Booking privacy when booking does not exist
    Given another driver looks up a non-existent booking
    When they are told it does not exist
    Then the outcome is "NOT_FOUND"
